Every file here was taken from cdnjs's copy of leaflet 1.9.4 and is byte-identical to it:

  leaflet.min.js  = https://cdnjs.cloudflare.com/ajax/libs/leaflet/1.9.4/leaflet.min.js
                    cdnjs's own minified build of leaflet 1.9.4. It is NOT upstream dist/leaflet.js with
                    the header removed: the two are different minifier outputs (different identifier
                    mangling), and dist/leaflet.js is what cdnjs serves as leaflet.js, header and
                    sourceMappingURL included. Same source release, different minification.
                    sha256 5c9aecfc30e4564519dbdcddcc53a418227dcc7568e619e9762ddcec7609ed47
  leaflet.css     = https://cdnjs.cloudflare.com/ajax/libs/leaflet/1.9.4/leaflet.css
                    (also byte-identical to dist/leaflet.css of leaflet@1.9.4)
                    sha256 a7837102824184820dfa198d1ebcd109ff6d0ff9a2672a074b9a1b4d147d04c6
  images/         = https://cdnjs.cloudflare.com/ajax/libs/leaflet/1.9.4/images/
                    (also byte-identical to dist/images/ of leaflet@1.9.4: layers.png, layers-2x.png,
                    marker-icon.png, marker-icon-2x.png, marker-shadow.png)

cdnjs's minifier drops the @preserve copyright header, so leaflet.min.js carries no notice of its own.
The BSD-2-Clause notice it would have carried is kept in LICENSE in this directory and reads:

